^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
unexpected expression
--
`struct __attribute__((packed)) P { ... }` (attribute between class-key
and name): the parser folded the attribute onto the struct but recorded
an EMPTY alignment (a default-constructed irept is not nil), so every
such class got a phantom explicit alignment -- "unexpected expression: "
during layout and, for structs with bit-fields or a trailing wider
member, a wrong size (4 for the 3-byte packed P).  The user's
`enum class : uint8_t` bit-field struct (Issue 7) was declared this
way.  Covers attribute before the name, after the body, and with
bit-fields.
